# Shemá - the Rhythm's log: which meeting of which period happened in which region (BE-10 · OBT-399)
#
# The log is a listening tracker, not an agenda: one entry per meeting, region and period, with the
# day it happened and its notes. Four things are worth running by hand before believing the rest:
#
#   1. THE SERVER DERIVES THE PERIOD. Post a day and read `period` in the answer: 2026-03-01 in the
#      bimonthly meeting is 2026-B2, in the quarterly 2026-Q1, in the semiannual 2026-H1. A body
#      that states its own `period` is a 422.
#   2. A SECOND LOG OF THE SAME PERIOD REPLACES THE FIRST. Post twice inside one bimester: the
#      first answers 201, the second 200, and the list has one entry with the second one's notes.
#   3. THE LOG IS NOT THE RESOURCE CIRCLE'S. Its notes are a pastoral reading of a team - the
#      reading the health assessment already withholds from `resourceCircle` - so that role gets a
#      403 on all three routes, in its own region.
#   4. `global` IS NOT A REGION. Every meeting GATE-02 kept is held per region; `scopeKey: global`
#      is a 422 that says so, for the global strategist too.
#
# The three meetings: bimestral_pi_campo, trimestral_pi_pontes, semestral_member_care. The Pulso
# Mensal is not here - its record is the submission received (GET /api/shema/forms/submissions) -
# and neither is the annual celebration, which is a report.
#
# Before running: seed the app and its roles, grant a coordinator and give it a region.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   (grant through app/services/authorization/grant_app_role.py, and set the region with
#    app/services/shema/set_region_scope.py - http/shema_session.http shows both)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Sign in as the regional coordinator
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "coord.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### The log, as far as this account reaches
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Log the bimonthly meeting - the answer carries the period the server derived (2026-B2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "meetingId": "bimestral_pi_campo",
  "scopeKey": "africa",
  "date": "2026-03-01",
  "notes": "Reviewed the forms of both teams; one asked for a follow-up call."
}

### Log it again inside the same bimester - 200, and the entry is replaced, not duplicated
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "meetingId": "bimestral_pi_campo",
  "scopeKey": "africa",
  "date": "2026-04-20",
  "notes": "Follow-up call held."
}

### A period stated by the client - 422: the server derives it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "meetingId": "bimestral_pi_campo",
  "scopeKey": "africa",
  "date": "2026-03-01",
  "period": "2026-B6"
}

### The Pulse is not a meeting - 422
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "meetingId": "pulso_mensal",
  "scopeKey": "africa",
  "date": "2026-03-01"
}

### Undo one period of one region - 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/meetings/log/bimestral_pi_campo/africa/2026-B2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
